101022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1061 618989 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3a6cc496-9cd7-5d8a-b41a-b6ed6646b019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101912 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101023 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1061 618992 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3d3e3cfa-978d-5956-a57b-742f51ee2e89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101913 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101024 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1064 "The region $\\textrm{R},$ shown below, is the area under the graph of $f(x) = 2x+1$ over the interval $[1,3].$ What is the height of the rectangle defined over the same interval that has the same area as $\\textrm{R}?$ \n\n![](images/01/01597200b1f0e147fa8c53b6301d0c8e37208b5a6cce64cf0d9859d1220d8385.png)\n\n \n\nUsing the formula for the area of a trapezoid, we have that\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\\textrm{Area}\\,(\\textrm{R}) = \\dfrac{1}{2}(3+7)(3-1)= 10.}\n$$\n\nFor the rectangle to have the same area, we must have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & =f(c)(3-1) \\\\ f(c) & =5 \\\\ 2c+1 & =5 \\\\ c & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can summarize what we've just done by saying that\n\n$$\n\\int_1^3 (2x +1)\\, \\textrm d x= f(2) \\cdot (3-1).\n$$\n\nThis is an example of the **mean value theorem for integrals**, which states:\n\n*If $f(x)$ is a continuous function on the closed interval $[a, b]$, then there exists a number $c$ in that interval such that*\n\n$$\n\\int_a^b f(x)\\, \\textrm d x = f(c) \\cdot (b-a).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1065 986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c1b3241c-c8fd-514f-aa8c-a000710896d4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102034 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1064 "The **average value** of a continuous function on a closed interval $[a,b]$ is given by\n\n$$\nf_\\textrm{avg} = \\dfrac{1}{b-a}\\int_a^b f(x) \\: \\textrm{d}x.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1065 988 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1cced554-b7fa-5fd4-b8b5-86c8e0bb4bc0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186102035 #edb/ref 1067 "The Average Value of a Function" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529665 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529925 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186529990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530042 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186530163 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186529990 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126428 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4a8fb9e3-9863-5703-95c1-0d8295fc07d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186531963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532385 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532433 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186532013 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186126440 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fded47ac-9666-5e9a-a118-02ceca041d7e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129318 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129318 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129318 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref